From: crazynucfan <127292955+crazynucfan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:35:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] arm64: negroni_defconfig: panic and reboot on lockups

A kernel that hangs on negroni only comes back if it panics: the APSS
watchdog belongs to the secure side on this phone (describing it sends
the kexec'd kernel to EDL), so nothing resets a wedged node. Turn the
soft and hard lockup detectors on with panic, the hard one in buddy
mode (there is no pseudo-NMI for the perf one), and panic on oops with
a 10 s reboot. The last two are what the kubelet sets at runtime, but
only once k3s is up; built in, a crash during boot reboots too.
test_lockup is there to drill each of them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/negroni_defconfig | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/negroni_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/negroni_defconfig
index 8accef6a9..71a3e1135 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/negroni_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/negroni_defconfig
@@ -1325,4 +1325,11 @@ CONFIG_CORESIGHT_STM=m
 CONFIG_CORESIGHT_CPU_DEBUG=m
 CONFIG_CORESIGHT_CTI=m
 CONFIG_MEMTEST=y
+CONFIG_PANIC_ON_OOPS=y
+CONFIG_PANIC_TIMEOUT=10
+CONFIG_SOFTLOCKUP_DETECTOR=y
+CONFIG_BOOTPARAM_SOFTLOCKUP_PANIC=1
+CONFIG_HARDLOCKUP_DETECTOR=y
+CONFIG_BOOTPARAM_HARDLOCKUP_PANIC=y
 CONFIG_DETECT_HUNG_TASK=y
+CONFIG_TEST_LOCKUP=m
